From 1185b9ff328871cae7e07445be7d2c9a2a5ae028 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VCKing101 <59761021+VCKing101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 13:53:51 +1030
Subject: [PATCH 57/62] Input: the script's second pad takes player 2's place
 from a real one

With a second player wanted, the gamepad scan stopped at the first spare pad
it found, so a real pad connected during a scripted run became player 2's
and the input script's second virtual pad was never opened. The scan now
offers every pad while a second player is wanted; the script's second pad
takes player 2's place from a real one, as its first pad does player 1's.

Checked with Dissidia 012 on Windows with a DualSense connected: a scripted
run opened the DualSense as player 2's, then the script's second pad in its
place.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 host/gpu/vulkan_renderer.cpp | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/host/gpu/vulkan_renderer.cpp b/host/gpu/vulkan_renderer.cpp
index 7c044b8..6009d4e 100644
--- a/host/gpu/vulkan_renderer.cpp
+++ b/host/gpu/vulkan_renderer.cpp
@@ -2358,8 +2358,10 @@ struct VulkanRenderer::Impl {
         int count = 0;
         SDL_JoystickID *ids = SDL_GetGamepads(&count);
         if (ids != nullptr) {
-            for (int i = 0; i < count && (gamepad == nullptr || (second_pad_wanted && gamepad2 == nullptr)); ++i)
-                open_gamepad(ids[i]);
+            // With a second player wanted, every pad is offered: the input
+            // script's second pad takes player 2's place from a real one
+            // found earlier, as its first pad does player 1's.
+            for (int i = 0; i < count && (gamepad == nullptr || second_pad_wanted); ++i) open_gamepad(ids[i]);
             SDL_free(ids);
         }
         if (gamepad != nullptr) return;
-- 
